  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Power Africa &#xe9;tend son partenariat solaire.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Power Africa:  International Finance Corporation (IFC) Public International Organization  (PIO) Scaling Solar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Africa Regional):  Power Africa will utilize FY 2021 funds to support the IFC Scaling Utility Scale Solar Photovoltaics Program (&quot;Scaling Solar&quot;) to unlock the utilization of one of sub-Saharan Africa&apos;s greatest power resources - solar.  The Scaling Solar Program builds stronger enabling environments in sub-Saharan Africa through:.Technical advice to support government clients to identify appropriate sites, perform feasibility and resource studies, and ensure local legal/regulatory compliance to reduce development costs and reduce specific project-related risksStandardized documents to lower transaction costs, ensure bankability, and lower riskSimple competitive tenders to drive competition in construction cost and cost of capitalPre-confirmed source of long-tenor, low-cost debt through stapled financing arranged and led by IFC, including (where necessary) blended concessional fundsAvailability of Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency (MIGA) and Partial Risk Guarantee coverage to lower off-taker and political risksStandardized approach across multiple countries to drive programmatic economies of scale and to attract top tier developers.Scaling Solar also increases competitive procurement of energy projects, namely solar generation projects, by providing streamlined procurement structures, documents, and technical expertise on generation procurement, which helps governments avoid unfavorable terms in bilateral generation deals...</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Financement du Bureau r&#xe9;gional africain de l&apos;Organisation mondiale de la sant&#xe9; (OMS/AFRO) pour le contr&#xf4;le des maladies et la sant&#xe9; reproductive en Afrique.</narrative>
  </description>
